.nh
.TH "ORBIT" "1" "Aug 2026" "Orbit Developer Platform" "Orbit Platform Manual"

.SH NAME
orbit-dev-routes - Generate the Caddyfile that serves native dev processes at \&.localhost


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBorbit dev routes [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Route every registry service with runs: mac and a localhost name (ports.yaml) to http://\&.localhost through Caddy, a reverse proxy to 127.0.0.1:\&. The default prints the Caddyfile on stdout; --write writes it to a path, --list prints a table, and --json prints the list as a JSON envelope.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for routes

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print the routes as a JSON envelope

.PP
\fB--list\fP[=false]
	print the routes as a table (NAME, URL, PORT, SERVICE) instead of the Caddyfile

.PP
\fB--root\fP=""
	workspace root holding handbook/agents/workspace/ports.yaml (default: the workspace containing the current directory)

.PP
\fB--write\fP=""
	write the Caddyfile to this path (parent directories are created) and print the path


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	Custom path to Orbit CLI configuration file


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBorbit-dev(1)\fP
